IMPORT prelude

-- Inquiries Act 2007 (Singapore) -- what a commission of inquiry (President, s 3) and a committee of inquiry (Minister, s 9) may
-- inquire into, how each must be composed (ss 4, 10), the chairperson's power over assessors (ss 7(3), 13(3)), and from the
-- Schedule: no ruling on liability (para 1(1)), the commission's extra enforcement powers (para 1(4)), suspension (para 2), the bar on
-- using a witness's evidence against them (para 4), the offences and contempt (paras 5 to 7), immediate sentencing for contempt by
-- commissioners (para 8), the right to an advocate (para 10), and which court "court" means (para 16).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IA2007.txt. The deposit labels
-- itself "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/4/2022"; the latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2021
-- (with effect from 1 April 2022, on Schedule para 10).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content: the
-- subject-matter limits, composition, offences and penalties, immunity-adjacent evidence rules and representation. Not encoded:
-- secretaries (ss 6, 12), the police role (s 8), the President's and Minister's discretions over terms of reference and time
-- (ss 3(2)-(4), 9(2)-(4)), rule-making (ss 15, 16), the transitional saving (s 17), the inquiry body's evidence-gathering powers
-- (para 1(2), (3), (5)-(8)), interpreters (para 3), the Public Prosecutor's aid (para 9), the Attorney-General's role (para 11),
-- protection and privilege (para 12), procedure (para 13), remuneration (para 14) and reports (para 15).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Inquiries Act 2007 -- inquiries`

DECLARE `Inquiry Body` IS ONE OF
    `a commission of inquiry`
    `a committee of inquiry`

§§ `3(1) and 9(1) -- what may be inquired into`

-- s 3(1): the President may issue a commission to inquire into "(a) the conduct of any officer or officers in the public service of
-- Singapore; (b) the conduct or management of any department of the public service or any public or local institution; or (c) any
-- matter in which an inquiry would, in the opinion of the President, be for the public welfare or in the public interest."
-- s 9(1): any Minister may appoint a committee to inquire into "(a) any accident or occurrence resulting in or involving death,
-- serious personal injury or serious property damage; (b) any occurrence that may endanger public safety or public health; (c) the
-- conduct or management of a ministry, department or statutory body falling under the responsibility of that Minister; or (d) the
-- conduct of any officer employed by or seconded to any such ministry, department or statutory body."
--
-- A committee has no catch-all "public interest" head; a commission has one, but only through the President's opinion. A commission
-- reaches an accident or a public-health danger only through that head (s 3(1)(c)).
DECLARE Subject IS ONE OF
    `the conduct of a public officer`
    `the management of a government department`
    `an accident causing death or serious injury or damage`
    `an occurrence that may endanger public safety or health`
    `another matter of public interest`

GIVEN `the body` IS AN `Inquiry Body`, `the subject` IS A Subject, `it falls under the appointing Minister's responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President thinks an inquiry is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subject is within the body's remit` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a commission of inquiry` THEN
        CONSIDER `the subject`
        WHEN `the conduct of a public officer` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the management of a government department` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `the President thinks an inquiry is in the public interest`
    WHEN `a committee of inquiry` THEN
        CONSIDER `the subject`
        WHEN `an accident causing death or serious injury or damage` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an occurrence that may endanger public safety or health` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the conduct of a public officer` THEN `it falls under the appointing Minister's responsibility`
        WHEN `the management of a government department` THEN `it falls under the appointing Minister's responsibility`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4(1)-(3) and 10(1)-(3) -- composition`

-- s 4(1): a commission "must consist of one or more persons (at least one of whom must be a person who is qualified to be a Judge of
-- the High Court)"; (2) where more than one, the President "must appoint one of the commissioners to be the chairperson"; (3) a sole
-- commissioner "is vested with the powers of the chairperson".
-- s 10(1)-(3): the same for a committee, with "qualified to be a District Judge" and the Minister appointing the chairperson.
GIVEN `the body` IS AN `Inquiry Body`, `members` IS A NUMBER, `members qualified to be a High Court Judge` IS A NUMBER, `members qualified to be a District Judge` IS A NUMBER, `a chairperson has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is properly composed` IF
        `members` AT LEAST 1
    AND (`members` EQUALS 1 OR `a chairperson has been appointed`)
    AND CONSIDER `the body`
        WHEN `a commission of inquiry` THEN `members qualified to be a High Court Judge` AT LEAST 1
        WHEN `a committee of inquiry` THEN `members qualified to be a District Judge` AT LEAST 1

§§ `7(3) and 13(3) -- terminating an assessor`

-- s 7(3): "The chairperson may at any time terminate the appointment of an assessor, but only with the consent of the President in the
-- case of an assessor appointed by the President." s 13(3) is the same for the Minister.
GIVEN `appointed by the appointing authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appointing authority consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chairperson may terminate the assessor` IF
    (NOT `appointed by the appointing authority`) OR `the appointing authority consents`

§§ `Schedule para 1(1) -- no ruling on liability`

-- para 1(1): an inquiry body "must not rule on and has no power to determine the civil or criminal liability of any person", but is not
-- inhibited by any likelihood of liability being inferred from the facts it determines or the recommendations it makes.
-- para 15(1): the report sets out the facts determined and the recommendations (where the terms of reference require them).
DECLARE Finding IS ONE OF
    `what the facts were`
    `a recommendation`
    `that a person is civilly liable`
    `that a person is guilty of an offence`

GIVEN `the finding` IS A Finding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inquiry body may make the finding` IF
    CONSIDER `the finding`
    WHEN `that a person is civilly liable` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `that a person is guilty of an offence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule paras 1(4) and 16 -- the court an inquiry body stands in for`

-- para 1(4): "In addition to the powers described in sub-paragraph (3), a commission of inquiry has the powers of the General Division
-- of the High Court for the purposes of giving effect to any order of imprisonment and enforcing the payment of any fine imposed."
-- No such sub-paragraph is given for a committee.
GIVEN `the body` IS AN `Inquiry Body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body has High Court powers to imprison and enforce fines` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a commission of inquiry` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- para 16: for a commission "a reference to a court is to be construed as a reference to the General Division of the High Court"; for a
-- committee, "a reference to a District Court".
DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `a District Court`

GIVEN `the body` IS AN `Inquiry Body`
GIVETH A Court
`the court referred to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a commission of inquiry` THEN `the General Division of the High Court`
    WHEN `a committee of inquiry` THEN `a District Court`

§§ `Schedule para 2 -- suspending an inquiry`

-- para 2(1): the chairperson may, "with the consent of the appointing authority", suspend an inquiry to allow for "(a) the completion
-- of any other investigation relating to any of the matters" or "(b) the determination of any civil or criminal proceedings
-- (including proceedings before a disciplinary tribunal)" arising out of them; (2) "whether or not the investigation or proceedings
-- have begun".
GIVEN `the appointing authority consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `to allow another investigation or proceedings on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chairperson may suspend the inquiry` IF
    `the appointing authority consents` AND `to allow another investigation or proceedings on the matter`

§§ `Schedule para 4 -- evidence not to be used against the witness`

-- para 4: "No evidence taken in the course of any inquiry is admissible as evidence in any proceedings against the person who gave the
-- evidence, other than proceedings, whether criminal or disciplinary, for an offence under this Act or an offence of giving or
-- fabricating false evidence under any written law."
-- The paragraph says nothing about proceedings against someone else; this rule decides only whether para 4 bars the evidence.
GIVEN `the proceedings are against the person who gave the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN, `for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `for giving or fabricating false evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 4 bars the evidence` IF
        `the proceedings are against the person who gave the evidence`
    AND (NOT (`for an offence under this Act` OR `for giving or fabricating false evidence`))

§§ `Schedule paras 5 to 7 -- offences and contempt`

-- para 5(1): during the course of an inquiry, (a) wilfully giving false evidence on oath or affirmation; (b) distorting or preventing
-- evidence; (c) "intentionally suppresses or conceals" or (d) "intentionally alters or destroys" a document "that is, and that the
-- person knows or believes to be, a relevant document" -- fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 7 YEARS or both.
-- para 6(1): hindering a summoned witness, or deterring a witness "by threats or coercion"; (2) wilfully threatening, insulting,
-- injuring or causing loss to a person for having given evidence -- the same $10,000 or 7 years.
-- para 7(1): contempt, including (a) insult or threat to a member while sitting; (c) wilfully interrupting the proceedings; (d)
-- "without lawful excuse" refusing an oath or affirmation; (e) "without lawful excuse" disobeying a summons; (f) as a witness, "without
-- lawful excuse" refusing to answer a relevant question; (2) contempt is an offence -- fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 2 YEARS or both.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `wilfully giving false evidence on oath`
    `concealing a relevant document`
    `destroying a relevant document`
    `hindering a summoned witness from attending`
    `deterring a witness by threats`
    `retaliating against a person for their evidence`
    `insulting a member while the body sits`
    `wilfully interrupting the proceedings`
    `refusing to take an oath`
    `disobeying a summons`
    `refusing to answer a relevant question`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is contempt` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `insulting a member while the body sits` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `wilfully interrupting the proceedings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing to take an oath` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disobeying a summons` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing to answer a relevant question` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Only paragraphs 7(1)(d), (e) and (f) carry the words "without lawful excuse".
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a lawful excuse is a defence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `refusing to take an oath` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disobeying a summons` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing to answer a relevant question` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
    (NOT `a lawful excuse is a defence` `the conduct`) OR (NOT `had a lawful excuse`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS 10000

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    IF `the conduct is contempt` `the conduct` THEN 2 ELSE 7

-- para 5(1)(c), (d) and 5(2): a document is "relevant" "if it is likely that the inquiry body would (if aware of the existence of the
-- document) wish to be provided with it". The offence needs intention, relevance, and the person's knowledge or belief of relevance,
-- all "during the course of an inquiry".
GIVEN `during the course of an inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN, `intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN, `the body would likely wish to have it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person knows or believes it relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `destroying the document is an offence` IF
    `during the course of an inquiry` AND `intentionally` AND `the body would likely wish to have it` AND `the person knows or believes it relevant`

§§ `Schedule para 8 -- commissioners punishing contempt`

-- para 8(1): where contempt "is committed in the presence of the commissioners sitting in commission, the commissioners may after
-- hearing the offender in the offender's defence pass sentence upon the offender immediately"; (2) in any other case they may summon
-- the offender to show cause. The paragraph speaks only of commissioners: it gives a committee of inquiry no such power.
GIVEN `the body` IS AN `Inquiry Body`, `committed in the presence of the sitting body` IS A BOOLEAN, `the offender has been heard in defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body may sentence for contempt immediately` IF
        `committed in the presence of the sitting body`
    AND `the offender has been heard in defence`
    AND CONSIDER `the body`
        WHEN `a commission of inquiry` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Schedule para 10 -- representation by an advocate`

-- para 10(1): a person "whose conduct is the subject of inquiry", or "who is in any way implicated or concerned in the matter under
-- inquiry, is entitled to be represented by an advocate at the whole of the inquiry"; (2) any other person may be represented "by
-- permission of the inquiry body".
GIVEN `their conduct is the subject of the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN, `implicated or concerned in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is entitled to an advocate` IF
    `their conduct is the subject of the inquiry` OR `implicated or concerned in the matter`

GIVEN `their conduct is the subject of the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN, `implicated or concerned in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `the inquiry body permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be represented by an advocate` IF
    `the person is entitled to an advocate` `their conduct is the subject of the inquiry` `implicated or concerned in the matter` OR `the inquiry body permits`
